pages.push(`<section class="page">${header('Public Value','What Residents Receive','The budget is more than a ledger. It is a service promise: what the County will deliver, what it costs, and how the public can see whether results improve.')}
<p class="lede">A typical homesteaded $250,000 home contributes about $687 to the County operating levy - supporting public safety, roads, parks, libraries, planning, environmental stewardship, courts, and other countywide services.</p>
<div class="stats">${stat('$687','Illustrative County Property Tax')}${stat('$345.2M','Net Service-Delivery Budget')}${stat('1,515','Budgeted FTE')}${stat('$71.3M','FY2027 Capital Program')}</div>
<h2>Public benefit, expressed as service</h2><div class="grid3">
<div class="card good"><strong>Safety and readiness</strong><p>Sheriff, fire support, emergency management, code compliance, courts, medical examiner, and beach safety services protect residents and visitors.</p></div>
<div class="card good"><strong>Mobility and infrastructure</strong><p>Road, drainage, bridge, pedestrian, wastewater, and facility investments preserve access and accommodate growth.</p></div>
<div class="card good"><strong>Quality of place</strong><p>Libraries, recreation, beaches, parks, environmental programs, housing assistance, and veteran services support daily life.</p></div></div>
<h2>Who helps pay?</h2><div class="grid2"><div class="card goldbar"><strong>Residents and property owners</strong><p>Property taxes and locally established fees support general services and dedicated activities. The property-tax example above is illustrative and excludes School Board, water management, and other taxing authorities.</p></div><div class="card goldbar"><strong>Visitors, users, and outside partners</strong><p>Tourist Development Taxes, charges for services, fuel taxes, grants, and intergovernmental revenues shift a meaningful share of cost away from the general property-tax base.</p></div></div>
<h2>How value is demonstrated</h2><p>Department pages pair each service with historical measures and an FY2027 target. The program pages that follow aggregate those services across organizational boundaries, while the capital chapter explains the public benefit expected from major assets.</p>
<p class="note" style="margin-top:.12in">The $687 illustration assumes $200,000 taxable value after a $50,000 homestead exemption and the 3.4347 operating millage. Individual tax bills vary.</p>${footer()}</section>`);

